# Test: RFC 9568 Accept_Mode reaches the dataplane. An Active router that is not
# the address owner accepts packets addressed to its virtual address only when
# the operator sets accept-mode true, and never otherwise.
#
# VALIDATES:
#   RFC 9568 Section 6.4.3 -- "It MUST accept packets addressed to the IPvX
#   address(es) associated with the Virtual Router if it is the IPvX address
#   owner or if Accept_Mode is True. Otherwise, it MUST NOT accept these
#   packets." The group here owns no virtual address (the parent holds
#   198.51.100.251, the group backs 198.51.100.1), so the leaf alone decides.
#   The proof is a UDP datagram sent to the virtual address on this host: a
#   packet addressed to a local address goes through the input hook, so a
#   listener bound to that address receives it exactly when the router accepts.
#   VIP-NOT-ACCEPTED and VIP-ACCEPTED are that observation, and the test flips
#   the leaf back to false so acceptance is proven to follow the leaf in both
#   directions rather than only to be switched on once.
#
#   RFC 9568 Section 6.4.3 -- the Active router still answers ARP for the virtual
#   address, which on Linux follows from the address being installed. So the
#   suppression is not "do not install the address": ACTIVE-WITH-VIP reads the
#   address back off the virtual-MAC macvlan while the router is refusing traffic
#   for it.
#
#   RFC 9568 Section 6.1 -- IPv6 Neighbor Solicitations and Advertisements MUST
#   NOT be dropped when Accept_Mode is False. ND-CARVE-OUT-BEFORE-DROP reads the
#   kernel rules and proves both ICMPv6 accepts sit ahead of the address drop,
#   which is where they have to be: the first matching rule takes the verdict.
#
#   Teardown -- removing the group takes the rules away with the address.
#   TEARDOWN-COMPLETE proves no drop rule outlives the group that asked for it,
#   which would silence the virtual address for whatever runs next.
#
# PREVENTS: the defect this test was written against, in which accept-mode
#   reached config parsing, the version rule and the show snapshot and nothing
#   else, so an Active ze router answered on the virtual address whichever way
#   the operator set the leaf. Also a filter that never withdraws, and a carve-out
#   placed after the drop, where it would do nothing.
#
# option=needs-linux: the proof needs macvlan creation, netlink address install
# and a real nftables ruleset. None of them exists on darwin. Runs as root in the
# QEMU Linux VM.
# caps=net-admin because the setup fixture creates the veth parent and the daemon
# programs netlink and nftables. Without the declaration an unprivileged Linux
# host does not skip: the calls are refused and the test fails for a capability
# the host never had (internal/test/runner/record_parse.go, option=needs-linux).
option=needs-linux:caps=net-admin
# option=exclusive: reconcileOwnedDevices (iface/config_apply.go) deletes every
# "ze:owned:" macvlan absent from ITS registry, so two ze daemons owning macvlans
# in one network namespace remove each other's devices. The group is named for
# the resource rather than for vrrp: any plugin registering an owned macvlan
# contends for the same alias namespace.
option=exclusive:group=iface-owned-macvlan


stdin=ze-bgp:terminator=EOF_CONF
interface {
	backend netlink;
	ethernet zeptam0 {
		unit 0 {
			ipv4 {
				address [ 198.51.100.251/24 ];
				vrrp {
					group lab {
						vrid 11;
						virtual-address [ 198.51.100.1 ];
						priority 200;
						accept-mode false;
						advertise-interval-milliseconds 1000;
					}
				}
			}
		}
	}
}
EOF_CONF

option=env:var=ze.log.vrrp:value=info

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze-test fixture vrrp/vrrp-accept-mode-setup
cmd=background:seq=2:exec=ze -:stdin=ze-bgp
cmd=foreground:seq=3:exec=ze-test fixture vrrp/vrrp-accept-mode-driver:timeout=120s
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stdout:contains=ACTIVE-WITH-VIP
expect=stdout:contains=ND-CARVE-OUT-BEFORE-DROP
expect=stdout:contains=VIP-NOT-ACCEPTED accept-mode-false
expect=stdout:contains=VIP-ACCEPTED accept-mode-true
expect=stdout:contains=VIP-NOT-ACCEPTED accept-mode-false-again
expect=stdout:contains=TEARDOWN-COMPLETE
expect=stderr:contains=vrrp: state change
